(7221492, 1114004, 67258, '<td valign="top">Lovely!</td>', 'Lovely!', '2014-05-28 05:23:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221493, 1113283, 67258, '<td valign="top">Good focus and depth of field, but the composition is off for me.</td>', 'Good focus and depth of field, but the composition is off for me.', '2014-05-28 05:24:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221494, 1113367, 67258, '<td valign="top">A pretty flower photographed with a lovely delicate touch.</td>', 'A pretty flower photographed with a lovely delicate touch.', '2014-05-28 05:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221495, 1113892, 67258, '<td valign="top">The bright sky competes with my attention, which is a great shame because there is some super light on the flowers.</td>', 'The bright sky competes with my attention, which is a great shame because there is some super light on the flowers.', '2014-05-28 05:26:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221496, 1113638, 67258, '<td valign="top">This scene was probably too contrasty to be effectively captured under minimal editing, at least without any fill flash to balance the light out.  Earlier or later in the day and it may have worked better.</td>', 'This scene was probably too contrasty to be effectively captured under minimal editing, at least without any fill flash to balance the light out.  Earlier or later in the day and it may have worked better.', '2014-05-28 05:27:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221497, 1113728, 67258, '<td valign="top">A bit of a shame about the bud in front of the stem - but otherwise, a good photo.</td>', 'A bit of a shame about the bud in front of the stem - but otherwise, a good photo.', '2014-05-28 05:28:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221498, 1113970, 67258, '<td valign="top">The light on the orchid is a little bright.</td>', 'The light on the orchid is a little bright.', '2014-05-28 05:29:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221499, 1113612, 67258, '<td valign="top">I like this very much.</td>', 'I like this very much.', '2014-05-28 05:33:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221500, 1113927, 67258, '<td valign="top">A little cramped, compositionally, but otherwise, a good entry.</td>', 'A little cramped, compositionally, but otherwise, a good entry.', '2014-05-28 05:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221501, 1113910, 67258, '<td valign="top">A beautifully delicate photograph of this clematis. Amongst my favourite of the challenge.</td>', 'A beautifully delicate photograph of this clematis. Amongst my favourite of the challenge.', '2014-05-28 05:35:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221502, 1113761, 67258, '<td valign="top">Absolutely delightful.  The contre jour really marks this out from the competition.</td>', 'Absolutely delightful.  The contre jour really marks this out from the competition.', '2014-05-28 05:38:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221853, 1113910, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Fantastic colors and light! These two flowers and both dainty and beautiful. Love the details and the soft pinks. Great bokeh for the flowers really pop off the natural green environment.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Fantastic colors and light! These two flowers and both dainty and beautiful. Love the details and the soft pinks. Great bokeh for the flowers really pop off the natural green environment.', '2014-05-28 21:36:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221854, 1113142, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the burst of purple that pops off of the orange backdrop. Nice complimentary light that illuminates the petals of the flower. Nicely done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the burst of purple that pops off of the orange backdrop. Nice complimentary light that illuminates the petals of the flower. Nicely done.', '2014-05-28 21:38:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7221856, 1113344, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Lovely take on bringing the beauty of the outside, inside. The light is also lovely for it illuminates the red roses and creates and interesting pattern on the wall behind. I like the color, but I also like the light and shapes from the glass vase to the table and window shade shadow that bring a comfortable home feel to this simple but elegant floral still life.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Lovely take on bringing the beauty of the outside, inside. The light is also lovely for it illuminates the red roses and creates and interesting pattern on the wall behind. I like the color, but I also like the light and shapes from the glass vase to the table and window shade shadow that bring a comfortable home feel to this simple but elegant floral still life.', '2014-05-28 21:43:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222389, 1113924, 7889, '<td valign="top">My favourite in the challenge. Love it !</td>', 'My favourite in the challenge. Love it !', '2014-05-29 20:28:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222394, 1113855, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Very pretty flower where the whites and reds of the delicate petals really pop off the backdrop. Lighting is fantastic. Negative space is good sometimes, but I can''t help but wonder if the composition would be even more stronger if it was done on the vertical allowing your subject to fully fill the frame and having the stem act as a strong leading line coming out of the bottom left corner at a diagonal.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Very pretty flower where the whites and reds of the delicate petals really pop off the backdrop. Lighting is fantastic. Negative space is good sometimes, but I can''t help but wonder if the composition would be even more stronger if it was done on the vertical allowing your subject to fully fill the frame and having the stem act as a strong leading line coming out of the bottom left corner at a diagonal.', '2014-05-29 20:55:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222395, 1113800, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>You have some very nice detail on the rose - most specifically I can see great texture on the petals. This is a good shot but there are a few things that can boast it into the high above average shot. First off it is just a touch too dark. Most likely you want the backdrop to stay a solid black so the white rose can really pop off the black. The white/cream rose needs just a punch more of vibrant contrast/brightness in the tones. You could either put a ''spotlight'' on just the white rose and/or move the black backdrop further away from subject so the light doesn''t fall on it to illuminate it.I also think the composition would be even stronger if you zoomed in closer to have your subject fill the frame bringing your audience closer to view all the lovely details. As it is now I think that there is  a little too much negative space at the top of the composition.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  You have some very nice detail on the rose - most specifically I can see great texture on the petals. This is a good shot but there are a few things that can boast it into the high above average shot. First off it is just a touch too dark. Most likely you want the backdrop to stay a solid black so the white rose can really pop off the black. The white/cream rose needs just a punch more of vibrant contrast/brightness in the tones. You could either put a ''spotlight'' on just the white rose and/or move the black backdrop further away from subject so the light doesn''t fall on it to illuminate it.I also think the composition would be even stronger if you zoomed in closer to have your subject fill the frame bringing your audience closer to view all the lovely details. As it is now I think that there is  a little too much negative space at the top of the composition.', '2014-05-29 21:04:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222396, 1113739, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Wow, you did a fantastic job on light painting these flowers with the minimal ruleset! Love the light play that illuminates the sides of the glass vase and makes those sunflowers glow. I wonder what this looks like in color?</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Wow, you did a fantastic job on light painting these flowers with the minimal ruleset! Love the light play that illuminates the sides of the glass vase and makes those sunflowers glow. I wonder what this looks like in color?', '2014-05-29 21:07:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222397, 1113506, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great pop of red hues of the tulips off the bokeh backdrop. I like the details in the tulip in the foreground. Lighting is superb in how it illuminates the petals of the main flower and towards the back. Composition framing is also wonderful in that my eye is instantly captured by the flower in the foreground and then travels in a leading line to each one behind it. Nice work!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great pop of red hues of the tulips off the bokeh backdrop. I like the details in the tulip in the foreground. Lighting is superb in how it illuminates the petals of the main flower and towards the back. Composition framing is also wonderful in that my eye is instantly captured by the flower in the foreground and then travels in a leading line to each one behind it. Nice work!', '2014-05-29 21:11:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222398, 1113955, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nice light, lovely colors that pop off the darker backdrop, and great textural details seen in these two flowers. Love how the bokeh backdrop both compliments the flowers and shows them off in their natural surroundings. My only suggestion is to mayhap either open up the shutter a bit more or lower the shutter speed to allow a little more light to brighten up the scene. It is lovely but could still use just a touch of brightness to make them pop even more.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nice light, lovely colors that pop off the darker backdrop, and great textural details seen in these two flowers. Love how the bokeh backdrop both compliments the flowers and shows them off in their natural surroundings. My only suggestion is to mayhap either open up the shutter a bit more or lower the shutter speed to allow a little more light to brighten up the scene. It is lovely but could still use just a touch of brightness to make them pop even more.', '2014-05-29 21:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222399, 1113922, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Really nice details showcasing the texture of the petals, the back of the green stalk, and the waterdrops. I like how you zoomed in close to really show your audience all those lovely details right down the variation of pale red/orange hues in the petals. Lighting is spot on too. Nicely done.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Really nice details showcasing the texture of the petals, the back of the green stalk, and the waterdrops. I like how you zoomed in close to really show your audience all those lovely details right down the variation of pale red/orange hues in the petals. Lighting is spot on too. Nicely done.', '2014-05-29 21:18:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222401, 1113709, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Love the bold pop of vibrant oranges and golds of these flowers. Very nice details in the texture of the petals of the main flower. Composition is strong bringing us close to appreciate the details of the flower as well as the color that really draws the eye in. Very lovely work.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Love the bold pop of vibrant oranges and golds of these flowers. Very nice details in the texture of the petals of the main flower. Composition is strong bringing us close to appreciate the details of the flower as well as the color that really draws the eye in. Very lovely work.', '2014-05-29 21:27:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222403, 1113974, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Very lovely and delicate blossoms. Love the bokeh backdrop that adorns the composition acting like dainty ''snowflakes''. I think the composition could be even stronger if you zoomed in (maybe 30% more) to bring your audience just a little bit closer so that the floral branch of the main focus *almost* fills the frame. I say almost because the backdrop really compliments the blossoms.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Very lovely and delicate blossoms. Love the bokeh backdrop that adorns the composition acting like dainty ''snowflakes''. I think the composition could be even stronger if you zoomed in (maybe 30% more) to bring your audience just a little bit closer so that the floral branch of the main focus *almost* fills the frame. I say almost because the backdrop really compliments the blossoms.', '2014-05-29 21:35:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222404, 1113821, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>This is clearly a top notch photo. Love the light, the composition, the colors, and all the fantastic and lovely details of the orchids in the planter resting on the table. This is a very well done floral still life that will most assuredly will be in the top 5. Excellent work!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. This is clearly a top notch photo. Love the light, the composition, the colors, and all the fantastic and lovely details of the orchids in the planter resting on the table. This is a very well done floral still life that will most assuredly will be in the top 5. Excellent work!', '2014-05-29 21:39:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222405, 1113664, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Absolutely stunning detail in the texture of the flower''s petals! Great color and light that really allows the color and details to visually pop of the green bokeh backdrop.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Absolutely stunning detail in the texture of the flower''s petals! Great color and light that really allows the color and details to visually pop of the green bokeh backdrop.', '2014-05-29 21:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222407, 1113373, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Fantastic colors and some nice details seen on this unique flower. Lighting is very good giving good contrasts and brightness to allow this flower to shine. I like how you have the flower almost fill the frame which allows your audience to appreciate the details of this unusual flower.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Fantastic colors and some nice details seen on this unique flower. Lighting is very good giving good contrasts and brightness to allow this flower to shine. I like how you have the flower almost fill the frame which allows your audience to appreciate the details of this unusual flower.', '2014-05-29 21:46:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222411, 1113965, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to bump up and comment.<br/> <br/>The light, the colors and the flower are the strong points of this shot. In general it is a good shot but it has potential to be stunner if a few things are done to strengthen the composition. First off bring your audience closer to the main focus - fill the frame so we can see all the lovely details of this lovely hued flower. It will also eliminate much of the distracting backdrop that the flower seems to be swimming in. Zooming in closer also has the advantage that if you keep sharp focus on the flower, and set the aperature to 5.6 (or lower) it will lower the Depth of Field so that the background has a nice blurred bokeh effect thereby allowing the flower to really pop visually. Also centering a straight and level subject within the composition generally doesn''t hold the eye''s attention for long - a little off center or at an angle where there are leading lines (i.e. the stem coming at a diagonal for an example) adds drama and some visual interest. Lastly, lower the shutter speed or the ISO just a little so (not to much for generally you have good light and contrasts) that you don''t blow out some contrast/details - the yellow center has some blown highlights. One way you could look to see if the subject is all around well lit/balanced is to use the camera histogram function.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to bump up and comment. The light, the colors and the flower are the strong points of this shot. In general it is a good shot but it has potential to be stunner if a few things are done to strengthen the composition. First off bring your audience closer to the main focus - fill the frame so we can see all the lovely details of this lovely hued flower. It will also eliminate much of the distracting backdrop that the flower seems to be swimming in. Zooming in closer also has the advantage that if you keep sharp focus on the flower, and set the aperature to 5.6 (or lower) it will lower the Depth of Field so that the background has a nice blurred bokeh effect thereby allowing the flower to really pop visually. Also centering a straight and level subject within the composition generally doesn''t hold the eye''s attention for long - a little off center or at an angle where there are leading lines (i.e. the stem coming at a diagonal for an example) adds drama and some visual interest. Lastly, lower the shutter speed or the ISO just a little so (not to much for generally you have good light and contrasts) that you don''t blow out some contrast/details - the yellow center has some blown highlights. One way you could look to see if the subject is all around well lit/balanced is to use the camera histogram function.', '2014-05-29 22:01:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222412, 1113761, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to bump up and comment.<br/> <br/>Absolutely it is the light that dances in the frame and illuminates all those fantastic details from the hairlike fuzz all along the stem to the delicate petals showing the veins in the petals. Great bokeh that allows the flower to shine in it''s natural environment. Nicely done!</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to bump up and comment. Absolutely it is the light that dances in the frame and illuminates all those fantastic details from the hairlike fuzz all along the stem to the delicate petals showing the veins in the petals. Great bokeh that allows the flower to shine in it''s natural environment. Nicely done!', '2014-05-29 22:06:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222446, 1113101, 150277, '<td valign="top">This is a gorgeous capture of a rose.  The background colors complement your subject nicely.</td>', 'This is a gorgeous capture of a rose.  The background colors complement your subject nicely.', '2014-05-29 23:42:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222448, 1113636, 150277, '<td valign="top">I am a fan of high key images, so I really enjoyed this shot.  I have never seen a green flask like that, and I love the rope (?) that is around the top.  Nicely done.</td>', 'I am a fan of high key images, so I really enjoyed this shot.  I have never seen a green flask like that, and I love the rope (?) that is around the top.  Nicely done.', '2014-05-29 23:43:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222452, 1113873, 150277, '<td valign="top">I have to admit that I missed the water drops the first time through.  The brilliant colors, especially that yellow, and the up-close and personal point of view made a strong impression on my on their own.  This photo really made me smile.  I think this is a great shot.</td>', 'I have to admit that I missed the water drops the first time through.  The brilliant colors, especially that yellow, and the up-close and personal point of view made a strong impression on my on their own.  This photo really made me smile.  I think this is a great shot.', '2014-05-29 23:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222454, 1113821, 150277, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully unique entry.  The grays and browns are beautiful and they really set off your white flower.</td>', 'Wonderfully unique entry.  The grays and browns are beautiful and they really set off your white flower.', '2014-05-29 23:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222455, 1113924, 150277, '<td valign="top">Fun shot that I can see framed on a wall.  I like the high key, and daisy''s are my favorite flower.  The one yellow center where the white petals aren''t visible (or are very hard to see) distracted a bit and kept this from being my favorite. But overall I enjoyed the photo.  Thanks.</td>', 'Fun shot that I can see framed on a wall.  I like the high key, and daisy''s are my favorite flower.  The one yellow center where the white petals aren''t visible (or are very hard to see) distracted a bit and kept this from being my favorite. But overall I enjoyed the photo.  Thanks.', '2014-05-29 23:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222456, 1113728, 150277, '<td valign="top">Great sharpness on your subject.  For some reason I found the green background a bit too vivid or strong.  You subject sure popped, but the background distracted just a bit.</td>', 'Great sharpness on your subject.  For some reason I found the green background a bit too vivid or strong.  You subject sure popped, but the background distracted just a bit.', '2014-05-29 23:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222457, 1114007, 150277, '<td valign="top">I found this shot interesting, but the longer I looked the more uncomfortable I became.  I felt a bit like the flower was being strangled or hurt.  Photographically this was a nice shot, the light was pretty.  That bit of aluminum pan near the top right was a bit distracting, and you left me a little sadder.</td>', 'I found this shot interesting, but the longer I looked the more uncomfortable I became.  I felt a bit like the flower was being strangled or hurt.  Photographically this was a nice shot, the light was pretty.  That bit of aluminum pan near the top right was a bit distracting, and you left me a little sadder.', '2014-05-29 23:52:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222458, 1113373, 150277, '<td valign="top">Nice pop of color, beautiful smooth background.  Well done.</td>', 'Nice pop of color, beautiful smooth background.  Well done.', '2014-05-29 23:53:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222459, 1114004, 150277, '<td valign="top">Nice capture, although the sideways stem bothered me a bit since I did not have anything to help me put it in perspective.</td>', 'Nice capture, although the sideways stem bothered me a bit since I did not have anything to help me put it in perspective.', '2014-05-29 23:54:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222798, 1113160, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The B&amp;W tones are well done. I can really see the lovely details of the texture of the petals of this flower. While the B&amp;W is a strong composition I wonder what it looks like in color.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The B&W tones are well done. I can really see the lovely details of the texture of the petals of this flower. While the B&W is a strong composition I wonder what it looks like in color.', '2014-05-30 15:49:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222799, 1113765, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Great light that really makes this larkspur shine. The purple hues really pop visually of the green and orange backdrop. The vertical crop not only brings us closer to appreciate the beauty of this flower, but it also complements the vertical orientation of the subject. Love all the details I can see right down to the ''veins'' in the petals.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Great light that really makes this larkspur shine. The purple hues really pop visually of the green and orange backdrop. The vertical crop not only brings us closer to appreciate the beauty of this flower, but it also complements the vertical orientation of the subject. Love all the details I can see right down to the ''veins'' in the petals.', '2014-05-30 15:52:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222801, 1113791, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Lovely burst of floral color in this shot. Love how the vibrant purples pop off the bright greens. I do think that there is one thing that could make the composition even stronger to further appreciate the delicate nature of this flower. Bring your audience closer, zoom in such that your main subject either fills the bottom 1/2 (giving less stem) and more of the allium''s in the backdrop as bokeh or have a horizontal presentation where the main flower dominates the left half of the frame while the second half has the negative space of the bokeh background complete with the complementry field of greens and purple alliums.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Lovely burst of floral color in this shot. Love how the vibrant purples pop off the bright greens. I do think that there is one thing that could make the composition even stronger to further appreciate the delicate nature of this flower. Bring your audience closer, zoom in such that your main subject either fills the bottom 1/2 (giving less stem) and more of the allium''s in the backdrop as bokeh or have a horizontal presentation where the main flower dominates the left half of the frame while the second half has the negative space of the bokeh background complete with the complementry field of greens and purple alliums.', '2014-05-30 15:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222802, 1113915, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>The red petals of this desert flower really pops off the pale almost pastel hues of the backdrop. Great light and love the details seen on the downy soft petals. I daresay that the composition could be even stronger by zooming in closer where the stem is coming out of the bottom right corner to act as a leading line for the eye to follow up and appreciate even more the details of this flower.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. The red petals of this desert flower really pops off the pale almost pastel hues of the backdrop. Great light and love the details seen on the downy soft petals. I daresay that the composition could be even stronger by zooming in closer where the stem is coming out of the bottom right corner to act as a leading line for the eye to follow up and appreciate even more the details of this flower.', '2014-05-30 16:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222853, 1113878, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>There are fantastic details from the textures on the petals to the yellow center of this flower. Composition is excellent in that the main subject fills the frame and brings us in to appreciate the details. There is one thing that would greatly improve the shot and that is either different lighting and/or setting the camera''s setting on vivid (if it has that function). The lighting (guessing it might have been taken in full shade) or mayhap the camera setting has the main colors of this flower a little on the dull and flat side. Looking at the thumbnail and at the larger picture as well it seems a little washed out when the colors should and could be more vivid. Making sure the lighting fully illuminates your subject not just to get good details but also (depending on subject and mood) make it visually pop is the one thing that would catapult this in the the high end of the scale.</td>', 'Voted earlier, bumping up, and coming back to comment. There are fantastic details from the textures on the petals to the yellow center of this flower. Composition is excellent in that the main subject fills the frame and brings us in to appreciate the details. There is one thing that would greatly improve the shot and that is either different lighting and/or setting the camera''s setting on vivid (if it has that function). The lighting (guessing it might have been taken in full shade) or mayhap the camera setting has the main colors of this flower a little on the dull and flat side. Looking at the thumbnail and at the larger picture as well it seems a little washed out when the colors should and could be more vivid. Making sure the lighting fully illuminates your subject not just to get good details but also (depending on subject and mood) make it visually pop is the one thing that would catapult this in the the high end of the scale.', '2014-05-30 20:07:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222857, 1113393, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>Nice bright colors and some details on the flower. Composition has the flower fill the frame but I think it would be stronger if you pulled back just a little to capture the full flower with a touch of negative space off to the left. It is not much but maybe a slightly higher shutter speed and/or higher aperature might yield stronger details texture in the pink petals (it is faint but there) and boast contrast in the white center as that a few on the top have blown highlights on my monitor (it is not too bad but just a touch here and there on the white center ''petals'' on the top left mostly)</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  Nice bright colors and some details on the flower. Composition has the flower fill the frame but I think it would be stronger if you pulled back just a little to capture the full flower with a touch of negative space off to the left. It is not much but maybe a slightly higher shutter speed and/or higher aperature might yield stronger details texture in the pink petals (it is faint but there) and boast contrast in the white center as that a few on the top have blown highlights on my monitor (it is not too bad but just a touch here and there on the white center ''petals'' on the top left mostly)', '2014-05-30 20:16:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222871, 1113474, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>I like the bold and vibrant yellows and oranges in this sunflower shot. There is also some nice detail in the texture of the petals. I think this is a good shot but has potential to be even better if a few things were done. First is that the center portion of the sunflower that is in the shot needs a bit more light. I am thinking that the petals are backlit to get the lovely colors to shine so either you would need to have a small spotlight (flash)light shining on the center portion of the flower or a small portable reflector to bounce the light onto the the area in shadow. Next is composition. You give your audience a great close-up to see details but in this case it is a little too close. Pull back just a little bit to allow the full sweep of the petals to flow out to the edges of the frame. The leading lines of the petals are cut off on the left and bottom left of the frame - it feels ''interuppted'' when I think it would better if it flowed freely to fill that side of the frame.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. I like the bold and vibrant yellows and oranges in this sunflower shot. There is also some nice detail in the texture of the petals. I think this is a good shot but has potential to be even better if a few things were done. First is that the center portion of the sunflower that is in the shot needs a bit more light. I am thinking that the petals are backlit to get the lovely colors to shine so either you would need to have a small spotlight (flash)light shining on the center portion of the flower or a small portable reflector to bounce the light onto the the area in shadow. Next is composition. You give your audience a great close-up to see details but in this case it is a little too close. Pull back just a little bit to allow the full sweep of the petals to flow out to the edges of the frame. The leading lines of the petals are cut off on the left and bottom left of the frame - it feels ''interuppted'' when I think it would better if it flowed freely to fill that side of the frame.', '2014-05-30 22:39:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222873, 1113884, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Fantastic light on the petals of the this flower. Love how it illuminates the petals allowing all the texture/veins to *really* pop visually. The black backdrop also allows the flower to stand out from it''s environment. The motion of the rain, while an interesting touch, seems out of place in the shot. Had the shot been done outside with greenery or natural environment it would be more natural (of course the rain would have to be coming from a hose or watering can because we know Mother Nature never co-operates with a photographer''s schedule:-) ) Here with the studio/indoor lighting on a black backdrop it just looks odd and out of place. The rain is a unique addition, but I think it draws too much attention away from your main subject rather than complementing it.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Fantastic light on the petals of the this flower. Love how it illuminates the petals allowing all the texture/veins to *really* pop visually. The black backdrop also allows the flower to stand out from it''s environment. The motion of the rain, while an interesting touch, seems out of place in the shot. Had the shot been done outside with greenery or natural environment it would be more natural (of course the rain would have to be coming from a hose or watering can because we know Mother Nature never co-operates with a photographer''s schedule:-) ) Here with the studio/indoor lighting on a black backdrop it just looks odd and out of place. The rain is a unique addition, but I think it draws too much attention away from your main subject rather than complementing it.', '2014-05-30 22:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7222874, 1113240, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment. <br/> <br/>I think the perspective and the light that really makes the colors pop on the flowers are the strong points of this composition. I find it interesting that you decided to include the barbed wire in the shot. I am thinking it was intentional to show the contrast between things of delicate beauty (the buttercup flowers) and things that are ugly (the barbed wire). However the composition of the barbed wire in the top corner seems haphazard and most would mistake it to have no meaning other than it was perhaps an oversight. Also there are so many flowers scattered throughout the scene that it confuses the audience to think that they are the main focus rather than on of the main actors in the scene. If indeed it was intentional I think this has potential if you framed and composed the shot better. First off to show your audience there is symbolic meaning to the barbed wire being placed in the shot you should have them act as leading lines by composing it that the wire cuts across the frame at a diagonal ending at the top left and bottom right corners (might take a bit of work positioning yourself to get the shot but it will definitely be worth it to signal strongly to your audience that it is meant to be in the shot). Next you could angle the shot to have a few of the yellow flowers also come at a diagonal coming out from the left side extending to the right. They would almost act like crossed swords with the barbed wire or as nature escaping the boundaries set by the wire to cross over to freedom on the other side. The placement of flowers may not happen naturally so you may have to ''cheat'' in that you would pick the flowers and then arrange them so that you would/could achieve the angle needed for the composition. This is just a suggestion based on an educated guess that you meant to include the barbed wire for a reason given that the title you choose serves as a clue.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment.  I think the perspective and the light that really makes the colors pop on the flowers are the strong points of this composition. I find it interesting that you decided to include the barbed wire in the shot. I am thinking it was intentional to show the contrast between things of delicate beauty (the buttercup flowers) and things that are ugly (the barbed wire). However the composition of the barbed wire in the top corner seems haphazard and most would mistake it to have no meaning other than it was perhaps an oversight. Also there are so many flowers scattered throughout the scene that it confuses the audience to think that they are the main focus rather than on of the main actors in the scene. If indeed it was intentional I think this has potential if you framed and composed the shot better. First off to show your audience there is symbolic meaning to the barbed wire being placed in the shot you should have them act as leading lines by composing it that the wire cuts across the frame at a diagonal ending at the top left and bottom right corners (might take a bit of work positioning yourself to get the shot but it will definitely be worth it to signal strongly to your audience that it is meant to be in the shot). Next you could angle the shot to have a few of the yellow flowers also come at a diagonal coming out from the left side extending to the right. They would almost act like crossed swords with the barbed wire or as nature escaping the boundaries set by the wire to cross over to freedom on the other side. The placement of flowers may not happen naturally so you may have to ''cheat'' in that you would pick the flowers and then arrange them so that you would/could achieve the angle needed for the composition. This is just a suggestion based on an educated guess that you meant to include the barbed wire for a reason given that the title you choose serves as a clue.', '2014-05-30 23:08:02.000000', NULL, 1),
